## A Royal Heritage

The **Royal Golf Club Mariánské Lázně** was founded in 1905 at the initiative of **King Edward VII of England**, who visited Marienbad regularly and was a passionate golfer. The club is the **oldest golf club in the Czech Republic** and one of the oldest in Central Europe.

Edward's influence on Marienbad extended far beyond golf — he transformed the town into the summer meeting place of European diplomacy. But the golf club remains his most visible legacy: a place where sporting excellence meets natural beauty.

## The Course

The 18-hole championship course sits on a **787-metre plateau** in the Slavkov Forest (Kaiserwald), offering a unique playing experience:

- **Par 72**, total length approximately 6,100 metres
- Set among pine forests on gently undulating terrain
- Natural hazards: forest edges, heathland, strategically placed bunkers
- Panoramic views over the town and the wooded hills beyond
- Special challenge: the altitude affects ball flight distances

The course is renowned for its **excellent condition** and harmonious integration with the natural landscape. Unlike many modern golf facilities, it was carefully woven into the existing woodland — the playing experience is defined by silence, nature and the expanse of the forest.

## The Clubhouse

The clubhouse, with its **Edwardian charm**, is a destination in its own right. The tastefully restored rooms preserve the atmosphere of the founding era and offer:

- Restaurant with terrace and panoramic views
- Bar and lounge
- Pro shop with equipment hire
- Changing rooms and showers
- Historical photographs and memorabilia

## Playing as a Guest

The Royal Golf Club **warmly welcomes visitors**. Here is what you need to know:

- **Season:** Mid-April to late October (weather dependent)
- **Green fee:** From approximately €80-120 depending on season and day
- **Equipment hire:** Full rental sets (clubs, trolley) available on site
- **Handicap:** Proof of handicap required; maximum handicap 36
- **Lessons:** PGA-qualified professionals for individual and group tuition
- **Booking:** Tee times can be reserved online or by telephone

## Tournaments

The club hosts several tournaments annually, including the traditional **King Edward VII Memorial Tournament**, which keeps the memory of the founder alive. The tournament season runs from May to September.

## Combining Golf and Spa

Many visitors combine a golf holiday with a spa stay — a perfect blend of sporting activity and recuperation. The Ensana Spa Hotels offer special **golf-and-spa packages** that combine green fees, transfers to the course and a daily wellness programme.

> "Golf in Marienbad is an experience unlike any other: the silence of the forest, the pure air at 787 metres, the feeling of playing a course that a king laid out."
